{
  "id": "EXO.18",
  "number": "18",
  "bookId": "EXO",
  "reference": "Exodus 18",
  "verseCount": 27,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "18",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "EXO 18"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "18",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moses' father-in-law Jethro, the priest of Midian, heard about everything that God had done for Moses and the people of Israel when he led them out of Egypt. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.1"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "2",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:2"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "2",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EXO.2.21+EXO.2.22"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ex 2.21–22",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So he came to Moses, bringing with him Moses' wife Zipporah, who had been left behind, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.2",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.2"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "3",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:3"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "3",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "ACT.7.29"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Acts 7.29",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and Gershom and Eliezer, her two sons. (Moses had said, “I have been a foreigner in a strange land”; so he had named one son Gershom.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18.3",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Gershom",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": This name sounds like the Hebrew for “foreigner”.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.3",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.3"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "4",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:4"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "4",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He had also said, “The God of my father helped me and saved me from being killed by the king of Egypt”; so he had named the other son Eliezer.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18.4",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Eliezer",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": ": This name sounds like the Hebrew for “God helps me”.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": ") ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.4",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.4"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "5",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:5"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "5",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Jethro came with Moses' wife and her two sons into the desert where Moses was camped at the holy mountain. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.5",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.5"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "6",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:6"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "6",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He had sent word to Moses that they were coming, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.6",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.6"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "7",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:7"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "7",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "so Moses went out to meet him, bowed before him, and kissed him. They asked about each other's health and then went into Moses' tent. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.7",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.7"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "8",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:8"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "8",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moses told Jethro everything that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had done to the king and the people of Egypt in order to rescue the Israelites. He also told him about the hardships the people had faced on the way and how the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " had saved them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.8",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.8"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When Jethro heard all this, he was happy ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and said, “Praise the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", who saved you from the king and the people of Egypt! Praise the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", who saved his people from slavery! ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now I know that the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " is greater than all the gods, because he did this when the Egyptians treated the Israelites with such contempt.” ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Jethro brought an offering to be burnt whole and other sacrifices to be offered to God; and Aaron and all the leaders of Israel went with him to eat the sacred meal as an act of worship.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.12"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The next day Moses was settling disputes among the people, and he was kept busy from morning till night. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When Jethro saw everything that Moses had to do, he asked, “What is all this that you are doing for the people? Why are you doing this all alone, with people standing here from morning till night to consult you?”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.14"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moses answered, “I must do this because the people come to me to learn God's will. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When two people have a dispute, they come to me, and I decide which one of them is right, and I tell them God's commands and laws.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Jethro said, “You are not doing it the right way. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You will wear yourself out and these people as well. This is too much for you to do alone. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Now let me give you some good advice, and God will be with you. It is right for you to represent the people before God and bring their disputes to him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "You should teach them God's commands and explain to them how they should live and what they should do. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But in addition, you should choose some capable men and appoint them as leaders of the people: leaders of thousands, hundreds, fifties, and tens. They must be God-fearing men who can be trusted and who cannot be bribed. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Let them serve as judges for the people on a permanent basis. They can bring all the difficult cases to you, but they themselves can decide all the smaller disputes. That will make it easier for you, as they share your burden. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "If you do this, as God commands, you will not wear yourself out, and all these people can go home with their disputes settled.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moses took Jethro's advice ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "and chose capable men from among all the Israelites. He appointed them as leaders of thousands, hundreds, fifties, and tens. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "They served as judges for the people on a permanent basis, bringing the difficult cases to Moses but deciding the smaller disputes themselves.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.26"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "EXO.18.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "EXO.18.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "EXO 18:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then Moses said goodbye to Jethro, and Jethro went back home.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
